{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T13:19:04.395Z","ordinal":36127,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0200a-63d8-7b21-adef-c3850aecebf7","turn_id":"01a08b53-6238-7541-940b-0de8e50181aa","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a7bb35bc-1463-4884-8c16-553bfe1ec75a","process_id":"58830","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","go build -o ./entire-brain ./cmd/entire-brain && sed -n '1,24p' /Users/thomi/.local/share/entire/evals/phase2/quality-run-v1-33808625/human-review.md && git diff --check && git status --short && git diff --stat"],"cwd":"file:///Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"go build -o ./entire-brain ./cmd/entire-brain && sed -n '1,24p' /Users/thomi/.local/share/entire/evals/phase2/quality-run-v1-33808625/human-review.md && git diff --check && git status --short && git diff --stat"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# Phase 2 Distillation Quality: Human Review\n\nYou do **not** need to read the complete audit archive. Review one item at a time with:\n\n```sh\nentire brain facts distill-quality adjudicate \\\n  --bundle <this-directory> \\\n  --adjudicator <your-id>\n```\n\nThe default is a balanced 20-item calibration batch in a full-screen terminal workspace. It isolates the exact statement the automatic filter judged, shows that statement first, and keeps surrounding conversation hidden unless you press `c`. Copilot, Cursor, and Claude appear as compact advisory answers with no human choice preselected. For each statement, answer whether it is potential long-term project knowledge, whether it has human authority, and whether its source is safe; use `y`, `n`, or `u`. Scroll with `j`/`k` or the arrow keys, use `p` for extra judge explanations, `x` to skip, `q` to stop, and `?` for help. A decision is written only after the confirmation step; every confirmed answer is saved immediately and the same command resumes without repeating it. Use `--plain` for the line-oriented accessibility or non-TTY fallback.\n\nRun `quality-run-v1:33808625a097f0e5ab411a5cddb92c337257a7b4c62c7fad7c53852dee919868` contains 719 packets: 221 critical, 456 with judge disagreement, 32 with invalid judge output, and 0 with missing judges. These are attention-routing counts, not human error labels.\n\nAfter calibration, continue in bounded sessions with `--queue critical|invalid|disagreement|clean|all --limit 1..100`. Model consensus never supplies a default decision.\n\nThe exhaustive evidence trail is in [`human-review-audit.md`](human-review-audit.md). It exists for audit and spot-checking; it is not a linear review task.\n M docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md\n M internal/cli/distill_quality_adjudicate_tui_v1.go\n M internal/cli/distill_quality_adjudicate_v1.go\n M internal/cli/distill_quality_adjudicate_v1_test.go\n M internal/cli/distill_quality_report_v1.go\n M internal/tui/quality_review.go\n M internal/tui/quality_review_test.go\n docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md                |  24 ++-\n internal/cli/distill_quality_adjudicate_tui_v1.go  | 151 ++++++++++++--\n internal/cli/distill_quality_adjudicate_v1.go      | 223 +++++++++++++++++----\n internal/cli/distill_quality_adjudicate_v1_test.go |  88 +++++++-\n internal/cli/distill_quality_report_v1.go          |   2 +-\n internal/tui/quality_review.go                     | 186 +++++++++--------\n internal/tui/quality_review_test.go                |  47 +++--\n 7 files changed, 555 insertions(+), 166 deletions(-)\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# Phase 2 Distillation Quality: Human Review\n\nYou do **not** need to read the complete audit archive. Review one item at a time with:\n\n```sh\nentire brain facts distill-quality adjudicate \\\n  --bundle <this-directory> \\\n  --adjudicator <your-id>\n```\n\nThe default is a balanced 20-item calibration batch in a full-screen terminal workspace. It isolates the exact statement the automatic filter judged, shows that statement first, and keeps surrounding c